ns about people based on the way they speak or dress? How can we understand the deeper meaning of a fairy tale or an episode of The Simpsons? What does macaroni and cheese mean, and why is it not on the menu at most upscale Manhattan eateries? This seminar introduces semiotics, the study of signs and the meaning-bearing sign systems they form; sign systems that include not only human language but also literature, painting, sculpture, film, music, dance and also such aspects of popular culture as advertising, fashion, food, and television, to name just a few. The diversity of semiotic systems provides many possibilities for thinking and writing critically about the world we live in.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall, spring.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "First-Year Writing Seminar.", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}, {"strm": 2692, "crseId": 365158, "crseOfferNbr": 3, "subject": "ROMS", "catalogNbr": "2021", "titleShort": "Humans and Climate Change", "titleLong": "Humans and Climate Change", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "SEM", "ssrComponentLong": "Seminar", "section": "101", "classNbr": 16377, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "02:55PM", "timeEnd": "04:10PM", "startDt": "01/24/2018", "endDt": "05/09/2018", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "kep44", "firstName": "Karen", "middleName": "Elyse", "lastName": "Pinkus"}], "pattern": "TR", "facilityDescr": "Rockefeller Hall 231", "bldgDescr": "Rockefeller Hall", "facilityDescrshort": "RCK231", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [], "campus